Conversion 2 of docs/research-notes/cumulative-coherence-rule-to-check-2026-08-21.md
(consumer half; the declaration + cross-check half shipped earlier today
as REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-1). Declaration replaces inference: an artifact
that declares a verdict_class inside the closed enum never reaches the
four substring token lists, which were patched at least six times
('disqualified:' — an honest negative — drew a critical flag this week).

_verdict_is_untrustworthy: partial retries; every other member is a
trustworthy terminal state. classify_artifact: positive -> Complete,
blocked -> Blocked, circular_positive/null/disqualified/partial ->
Research Finding. circular_positive deliberately does NOT label
Complete — an honest circular win reading as a research win downstream
is the exp6478 gap the enum closes — and the declaration also beats the
retro_*_closed upgrade. Principle-wrapped declarations are unwrapped
(QA-layer origin bug #2 shape). Out-of-enum values fall through to the
legacy path unchanged; the token lists stay as the fallback for the
historical free-text corpus.

Fallback enum copies are duplicated on purpose and pinned equal to
adversarial_verify._VERDICT_CLASSES by test. Mutations: enum branch
disabled -> RED, circular_positive mapped to Complete -> RED; restored
GREEN (7 new tests; 84 with neighbors).

